esentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an amount of money to be paid as a punishment for a crime or other offence"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You just need to bring change for the parking meter so I don't get a fine. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about beliefs, opinions and colloquial expressions."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to come by"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to come for a short visit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  She's coming by this weekend to look at the recipes and the cookbook and make a shopping list."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "java"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "coffee"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm paying for my java."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to give someone a hand"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to help someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Does she still want to give you a hand with your cleanse?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stoked"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very excited or thrilled"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm stoked!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be a blast "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be a lot of fun"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This is going to be a blast. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Homographs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can build your vocabulary by paying attention to special words which may have different meanings depending on how they are used."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hold on just a <span class=\"strong\"> second </span>\u2026 I'm paying for my java."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you learn new words, sometimes one word will have different meanings (even with the same spelling). These words are called homographs.<br />Some homographs have the same spelling and pronunciation but different meanings. These are called homonyms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some homographs include:<br /> <span class=\"strong\">ball</span> &rarr;  round object, dance<br />  <span class=\"strong\">bear</span> &rarr;  animal, tolerate<br />  <span class=\"strong\">box</span> &rarr;  container, fight<br />  <span class=\"strong\">can</span> &rarr;  container, able to<br />  <span class=\"strong\">colon</span> &rarr;  body part, punctuation<br />  <span class=\"strong\">date</span> &rarr;  something on the calendar, appointment, fruit<br />  <span class=\"strong\">fan</span> &rarr;  someone who admires something, something to keep a room cool<br />  <span class=\"strong\">gum</span> &rarr;  part of mouth, something to chew<br />  <span class=\"strong\">mole</span>&rarr;  animal, spot on one's body<br />  <span class=\"strong\">ring</span> &rarr;  circle, call, sound of a bell<br />"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the examples of homographs from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you talk to Amy a <span class=\"strong\"> second </span> time?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The staff person who needed the weekend off had to <span class=\"strong\"> change </span> her plans."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You just need to bring <span class=\"strong\"> change </span> for the parking meter."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't have to <span class=\"strong\"> close </span> the restaurant on Friday. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Amy's <span class=\"strong\"> close </span>to me."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We <span class=\"strong\">can </span>use my car to carry all the heavy <span class=\"strong\">can</span>s."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reduction of Function Words"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You sometimes pronounce words differently in speaking because of assimilation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you talk to Amy a second time?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Assimilation refers to when two sounds come together to make a new sound. You do this when you are speaking and the words link to each other in your sentences; thus, reducing the sounds. The pronunciation that results is different from the individual sounds of the words when said separately."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the following examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Woul<span class=\"underline\">d y</span>ou</span> like some coffee? <br />  Why<span class=\"strong\"> don'<span class=\"underline\">t y</span>ou</span> eat meat? <br />  Come and <span class=\"strong\">kis<span class=\"underline\">s y</span>our</span> mother."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Would you</span> like some coffee? </span> &rarr;/wouldja like some coffee/<br />  <span class=\"italic\">Why <span class=\"strong\">don't you</span> eat meat? </span> &rarr;/why doncha eat meat/<br />  <span class=\"italic\">Come and <span class=\"strong\">kiss your</span> mother. </span>&rarr;/come and kisshyur mother/"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We might still need your help with some of the recipes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What do you think about this idea?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We can take this time to catch up and also get you some new and improved eating habits."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I promise you won't miss your coffee."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, make a list of as many homographs as you can think of."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the homographs on small pieces of paper. Write one homograph per piece of paper."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner or a small group, take turns drawing a piece of paper from the pile. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Hold up the paper for your partner to see. Your partner will make two sentences that show the two meanings of the word on the paper. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose two pieces of paper and write 2 sentences for each one."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of homographs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make sentences that show the two meanings of each homograph."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write sentences using two of the homographs."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le07ob04re1img01.jpg"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about beliefs and opinions and use colloquial expressions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say and use words that are spelled the same but are pronounced differently and have a different meaning."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can link two sounds to make a new one."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Are you or have you ever been vegetarian? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think that vegetarianism is a healthy diet? Why or why not?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Pronunciation Spot: Should we give up meat?"}], "id": 0}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}],